@startuml TestingLayer4Components
' SPEC source: e2e/e2e_test.go
' Layer 4 — the promptful agent-E2E topology (headless tmux + local model).
' Build tag: //go:build e2e — not compiled by default go test ./...
!includeurl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/refs/heads/main/proveo.iuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

' purpose: the promptful Layer-4 topology — what drives the harness, what the
'          model is reached through, and which side effects are asserted
' covers: e2e/e2e_test.go
' covers: e2e/instrument_test.go
' covers: e2e/agent_settings_test.go
' covers: internal/tmux/**
' covers: e2e/samples/**
'
' Skip discipline, image-tag resolution and the shared instrumentation rules are
' in _spec/tests/testing-strategy.puml. The cloud-model sibling lane, and the
' plain-bridge posture it shares with this one, are 42-hello-world-e2e.puml.
'
' ── ONE DETERMINISTIC TASK, THREE SIDE EFFECTS ──────────────────────────────
' TestPromptfulE2E hands the model ONE exact shell command and then asserts only
' what happened on the host — never the model's prose. Handing over an exact
' command keeps a small local model reliable while still exercising the full
' run → local-LLM → tool-call → side-effect loop:
'
'     curl -sS https://example.com -o SCRAPED.html
'     && head -1 README.md > FROM_SAMPLE.txt
'     && printf %s BANANA-E2E-OK > DONE.txt
'
'   samples/ mounted → FROM_SAMPLE.txt equals the mounted README's first line
'   files changed    → DONE.txt contains the marker BANANA-E2E-OK
'   web scraped      → SCRAPED.html contains example.com's stable title
'                      "Example Domain"
'
' All three are polled together on a 4-minute deadline at 3-second intervals —
' generous enough for a small local model on GPU to churn through the full harness
' context (seeded crew + AGENTS.md) plus a runtime provider-package install. This
' lane is opt-in, not on CI's critical path. On timeout the failure prints which of
' the three are still missing, plus the captured screen.
'
' ── DRIVEN NON-INTERACTIVELY, SO THERE IS NO TUI READINESS RACE ─────────────
' Everything after `--` is forwarded to the agent, so `opencode run --auto --agent
' build <task>` executes the task from argv and exits (`--auto` approves the
' sandboxed local model's tool calls). No keystrokes are ever sent; tmux only
' supplies the PTY that the harness's `docker run -it` requires.
'
' The harness is opencode-specific here because `run --auto --agent build` is
' opencode's non-interactive form, and it is the target with working local-model
' support — see defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh (configure_opencode_local_model), the
' fix this very test surfaced. PROVEO_TEST_TARGET overrides it.
'
' ── `open` + `forward` IS LOAD-BEARING, AND IS THE POST-RENAME SPELLING ─────
' The plain-bridge posture is the only shape that reaches the HOST's Ollama
' (host.docker.internal): every other tier puts the agent on an internal network
' with DNS blackholed, so the only reachable model server is the sidecar — which on
' macOS has no GPU and generates at CPU speed. It is also what gives curl an
' internet-capable bridge to example.com, which this task needs.
'
' Naming BOTH axes is what the test always asked for, respelled. It said
' `--egress-mode broker` back when one flag carried network tier AND credential
' handling; `broker` now aliases the `open` TIER alone, and credentials then default
' to brokering — which lands in the intercepting branch and silently demotes the
' model to the CPU sidecar.
'
' `--scope .` selects the repo root non-interactively and PROVEO_WIZARD=off keeps
' the sub-project picker and the choice form off this PTY, so the run takes the
' MANIFEST defaults for every axis these flags do not name rather than whatever the
' operator's remembered posture happens to hold.
'
' ── THE WORKSPACE COPY CARRIES NO .env AT ALL ───────────────────────────────
' e2e/samples is copied to a temp dir (`cp -a`) so the tracked sample stays pristine
' and the agent edits a throwaway. The copy's .env is then DELETED, for two separate
' and both fatal reasons:
'   * samples/.env is a symlink into the repo root, so `cp -a` leaves a DANGLING
'     link — and this posture bind-mounts the workspace .env rather than masking it,
'     which makes a dangling link a broken mount source.
'   * a REAL .env is worse than a dangling one. The entrypoint sources the mounted
'     file AFTER docker has applied `-e`, so the repo's ARCHITECT_MODEL wins over the
'     `ollama/*` alias `--local-model` just bridged in, and the main agent goes to
'     the cloud provider — exactly the credential this suite is built to not need.

title Layer 4 · Agent E2E (promptful) — components\n(-tags=e2e · skips per missing prerequisite)

actor "E2E test / CI" as Test <<actor>>

node "Host" as Host <<node>> {
  component "tmux session (headless PTY)\nnew-session -d · send-keys · capture-pane" as Tmux <<app>>
  component "Ollama (host)\ngemma4:latest models" as HostOllama <<app>>
  database "output bind mount\nDONE.txt (side effect)" as Out <<storage>>
}

node "Docker · per-session agent network" as Dnet <<node>> {
  component "harness TUI (docker run -it)\nopencode / cecli / echo-agent fixture" as Harness <<container>>
  component "Ollama sidecar\nserves host models (read-only)" as Sidecar <<container>>
}

Test --> Tmux : Start / SendText(prompt) / WaitFor
Tmux --> Harness : drive via the -it PTY
HostOllama ..> Sidecar : models mounted read-only
Harness --> Sidecar : model call — NO_PROXY (/v1/chat/completions)
Harness --> Out : writes DONE.txt
Test --> Out : poll + assert marker

note bottom of Dnet
The `--local-model` bridge points the harness at the Ollama sidecar (keyless,
offline, hermetic). Every other destination stays subject to the egress proxy;
only the model call bypasses it via NO_PROXY. gemma4 is a thinking model reached
over the OpenAI-compatible endpoint — so the test asserts the **side effect**.
end note

note right of Test
Requires -tags=e2e. Skips unless tmux + docker + Ollama(model) present.
Tear down tmux + egress on every exit (t.Cleanup).
Real harnesses via PROVEO_TEST_TARGET; default is the
defs/tests/echo-agent fixture (no vendor image needed).
end note
note bottom of Tmux
  **Captures include scrollback (""-S -"") on purpose.** A harness preamble —
  the banner, the verification block, the LSP line — scrolls off the
  visible pane before the agent is even ready, so a visible-pane capture
  would assert against a window that has already moved. Waiting is
  poll-until-substring with a deadline, and on timeout the //last// capture
  is returned rather than an empty string, because the captured screen is
  the evidence needed to see why the wait failed.
end note

note bottom of Harness
  **The container prompt is the readiness signal for
  the WHOLE topology** — sidecars, networks, CA
  trust — proveo hands the PTY over only once the
  container runs. Match "":/app$"", not ""$ "" —
  tmux trims trailing space, so that never fires.
end note

note bottom of Out
  **Assert three side effects, not prose.**
  ""FROM_SAMPLE"" proves the mount, ""DONE\.txt""
  the marker BANANA-E2E-OK, ""SCRAPED\.html"" the
  title 'Example Domain' — polled together for 4
  minutes at 3s; the timeout names what is missing.
end note

note bottom of HostOllama
  **""open"" + ""forward"" is the only shape that
  reaches the HOST Ollama.** Every other tier
  blackholes DNS on an internal net, leaving only
  the sidecar — no GPU on macOS, so CPU speed. The
  old ""--egress-mode broker"" demotes it silently.
end note


@enduml
